You are bootstrapping FORGE — a self-hosted personal gym and workout tracking web app. 
FORGE is a companion/sister app to SPENCE (a kitchen inventory and nutrition tracker). 
It lives at /srv/jaaaames.com/forge/ and is inspired by the 'Strong' iOS app 
(https://help.strongapp.io/) but stripped to just core workout tracking and data 
presentation. No social features, no GIF library, no external integrations.

== INSPIRATION: SPENCE ==

FORGE should copy these patterns wholesale from SPENCE (/srv/jaaaames.com/spence/):

AUTH:
- Same single-key session auth pattern as core/auth.php. 
- Key loaded from getenv('FORGE_ACCESS_KEY') or a non-committed credentials file.
- Include auth.php as the FIRST line of every page AND every API endpoint.

DB:
- PDO SQLite3, same pattern as core/db_helper.php.
- get_db_connection() in core/db_helper.php returns PDO with ERRMODE_EXCEPTION and 
  busy_timeout 5000.
- Timezone: Australia/Sydney via date_default_timezone_set().

API PATTERN:
- POST-only JSON endpoints in core/ (e.g. core/api.php).
- All actions dispatched via $_POST['action'].
- Wrap everything in try/catch, return {'status':'error','message':'...'} on failure.
- Use PDO prepared statements everywhere.

UI:
- Bootstrap 5.3 dark theme. Background #121212, cards #1a1a1a, border #333, 
  accent color per module (define a per-page accent, like SPENCE uses per data-context).
- Sticky top navbar, same layout as core/header.php. Brand name "FORGE" in bold 
  with accent color.
- Font-weight 900 labels in uppercase, monospaced stats, muted secondary labels.
- Vanilla fetch() for all AJAX — no jQuery.
- Bootstrap Icons (bi-*) for all iconography.
- Chart.js for all data visualisation (loaded from CDN).

FILE STRUCTURE (mirror SPENCE):
/forge/
  index.php               — Dashboard (recent workouts, weekly volume, quick PR summary)
  core/
    auth.php              — Session auth
    db_helper.php         — PDO connection + helper functions
    api.php               — CRUD: exercises, workouts, sets, templates
    progress_api.php      — 1RM estimates, PR history, volume queries
  workout/
    index.php             — Active workout logger (the core UX)
  history/
    index.php             — Past workouts list + detail view
  exercises/
    index.php             — Exercise library (browse, add custom)
  progress/
    index.php             — Progression charts per exercise, volume trends
  templates/
    index.php             — Workout templates (create, edit, start from template)
  settings/
    index.php             — User preferences (units kg/lbs, default rest timer, 
                             progression scheme)
  database/
    schema.sql
    forge_empty.db        — Blank template committed to git
  .gitignore              — forge.db, uploads/, credentials.env

== DATABASE SCHEMA ==

exercises (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  name TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,
  category TEXT,              -- 'Barbell', 'Dumbbell', 'Machine', 'Cable', 
                              --  'Bodyweight', 'Cardio', 'Other'
  muscle_primary TEXT,        -- 'Chest', 'Back', 'Legs', 'Shoulders', 'Arms', 
                              --  'Core', 'Glutes', 'Cardio'
  muscle_secondary TEXT,
  is_custom INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
  notes TEXT
)

workouts (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  name TEXT,
  template_id INTEGER REFERENCES templates(id),
  started_at DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  finished_at DATETIME,
  notes TEXT,
  bodyweight_kg REAL          -- optional snapshot, can pull from SPENCE vitals
)

workout_sets (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  workout_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES workouts(id),
  exercise_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES exercises(id),
  set_number INTEGER,
  set_type TEXT DEFAULT 'working',  -- 'warmup', 'working', 'dropset', 'failure'
  weight_kg REAL,
  reps INTEGER,
  rpe REAL,                   -- Rate of Perceived Exertion 6.0–10.0
  -- Cardio fields (null for strength):
  duration_sec INTEGER,
  distance_km REAL,
  notes TEXT
)

templates (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  name TEXT NOT NULL,
  notes TEXT,
  created_at DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
)

template_exercises (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  template_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES templates(id),
  exercise_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES exercises(id),
  order_num INTEGER,
  target_sets INTEGER,
  target_reps_min INTEGER,
  target_reps_max INTEGER,
  target_rpe REAL,
  progression_scheme TEXT DEFAULT 'double', -- 'linear', 'double', 'rpe'
  progression_increment_kg REAL DEFAULT 2.5
)

personal_records (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  exercise_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES exercises(id),
  weight_kg REAL,
  reps INTEGER,
  estimated_1rm REAL,
  achieved_at DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
)

== KEY DOMAIN LOGIC ==

1RM ESTIMATION (implement in progress_api.php and inline JS):
  - Epley:   estimated_1rm = weight × (1 + reps / 30)
  - Brzycki: estimated_1rm = weight / (1.0278 − 0.0278 × reps)
  - Use Epley as default. Only calculate for reps > 1 and reps <= 12.
  - Auto-insert/update personal_records after every set save if estimated_1rm 
    exceeds current record.

PROGRESSION SUGGESTIONS (in progress_api.php):
  - 'linear': After a successful session (hit all target reps), suggest 
    +increment_kg next session.
  - 'double': Target is rep range (e.g. 3×8-12). If all sets hit top of range, 
    suggest +increment_kg and drop back to bottom of range. Otherwise suggest 
    same weight, aim for more reps.
  - 'rpe': If last session average RPE < target_rpe - 1, suggest +2.5kg. 
    If RPE > target_rpe, suggest same or -2.5kg.
  Show suggestion as a banner when starting a workout from a template.

WORKOUT LOGGER UX (workout/index.php — the most important page):
  - Persistent in-progress workout state stored in the DB (started_at set, 
    no finished_at yet).
  - Exercises listed vertically. Each exercise has a set table with columns: 
    Set# | Previous (last session weight×reps) | Weight | Reps | RPE | ✓
  - "Previous" column auto-populated from most recent workout_sets for that 
    exercise — crucial for continuity.
  - Add Set button appends a row. Long-press or swipe on set row to delete.
  - Rest timer: configurable countdown (default 90s), shows after ticking a set.
  - "Finish Workout" button sets finished_at, calculates total volume (sum of 
    weight × reps per working set), updates PRs.

PROGRESS CHARTS (progress/index.php using Chart.js):
  - Per-exercise: estimated 1RM over time (line chart), volume per session 
    (bar chart), weight used at specific rep count over time.
  - Overview: total weekly volume (bar chart), workout frequency heatmap 
    (calendar-style using a canvas grid), muscle group distribution (donut chart 
    from last 30 days).

EXERCISE LIBRARY:
  - Pre-seed with ~50 common exercises (barbell squat, deadlift, bench press, 
    OHP, row, pull-up, etc.) on first run — detect empty exercises table and 
    INSERT the seed data.
  - Custom exercises can be added. is_custom = 1.

== WHAT TO BUILD FIRST ==

Build in this order:
1. core/ (auth, db_helper, api, progress_api) + database/schema.sql
2. workout/index.php — the active logger (most critical, most used)
3. history/index.php
4. progress/index.php with Chart.js charts
5. exercises/index.php
6. templates/index.php
7. Dashboard index.php
8. settings/index.php

== WHAT NOT TO BUILD ==

- No user accounts (single user like SPENCE)
- No exercise GIF/video integration
- No Apple Health / Google Fit sync
- No social features
- No paid tiers or premium gates
- No workout sharing
- No barcode scanning (not relevant)
- No push notifications

== LINK TO SPENCE ==

FORGE and SPENCE are sister apps. Cross-link them in their navbars 
(a small "SPENCE" link in FORGE's nav pointing to /spence/, and vice versa). 
The visual language must be consistent: same dark theme, same Bootstrap 5.3 
version, same font stack, same uppercase bold label style. The accent color 
for FORGE is #FF5722 (deep orange — contrasts with SPENCE's #00A3FF blue).

